WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.220
Hi, I'm Phil from BBC Learning English.

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:07.779
I'm going to tell you three facts about 'the'.

00:00:07.779 --> 00:00:11.064
We use 'the' when referring to a specific thing

00:00:11.064 --> 00:00:14.130
and both you and the person you're talking

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:17.560
to know which one you mean. Please pass me

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.980
the milk.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.560
We can see the bottle so we know

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:25.330
it's that  one. Number 2...

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:30.710
We don't use 'the' when we're talking about something

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:33.590
in general. For example, I love chocolate.

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:36.090
Number 3...

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:39.322
We don't use 'the' when it doesn't matter which

00:00:39.322 --> 00:00:41.190
thing we're talking about.

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:44.684
We usually use 'a' or 'an', here. Give me a cup

00:00:44.684 --> 00:00:47.262
of tea, I don't care which cup,

00:00:47.262 --> 00:00:49.930
any cup will do.

